---
import Head from "@components/Head.astro";
import { url } from "@lib/utils";
import "maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css";
import "../styles/assignment04.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <Head title="The Temporary Forest - a field index by Mere" description="Vacant land across New York City, with fourteen close readings of parcel history and 2022 vegetation response in East New York." />
  </head>
  <body class="assignment-four">
    <a class="a4-skip" href="#field-notes">Skip to the field notes</a>
    <div class="field-index" id="field-index" data-base={import.meta.env.BASE_URL}>
      <aside class="field-notes" id="field-notes" aria-label="Project story and map controls">
        <div class="field-brand">
          <p class="field-byline">an unfinished atlas by Mere</p>
          <h1>the temporary<br />forest</h1>
          <p class="field-intro">A vacant-lot label tells us how land is recorded. It tells us much less about its surface, its past, or what might grow there.</p>
          <nav class="field-scales" aria-label="Choose a geographic scale">
            <button type="button" data-scale="city" aria-pressed="true">the city</button>
            <button type="button" data-scale="study" aria-pressed="false">East New York</button>
            <button type="button" id="open-surfaces" aria-pressed="false">the surfaces</button>
          </nav>
        </div>

        <section id="city-reading" class="city-reading">
          <h2>Vacant land, 2026</h2>
          <p>The 2026 PLUTO release records <strong>24,663 vacant tax lots</strong> across the five boroughs. This map can locate 24,213 of them. The remaining records have missing or empty boundaries.</p>
          <p>The pale green shapes are administrative records. Their colour does not say whether the land is bare, overgrown, accessible, or forested.</p>
          <div id="borough-list" class="borough-list" aria-label="Vacant tax lots by borough"></div>
          <p class="marginal-note">A place to begin, rather than an ecological inventory.</p>
          <button type="button" class="text-action leaf-action" id="enter-study">Look closely in East New York</button>
        </section>

        <section id="study-reading" class="study-reading" hidden>
          <h2>The East New York sample</h2>
          <p>254 matched vacant parcels formed the pilot screening set. The 36 largest were read against two archival years; 14 had histories suitable for this descriptive comparison with 2022 imagery.</p>

          <fieldset class="field-filter">
            <legend>Look at</legend>
            <label><input type="radio" name="reading" value="vegetation" checked /> vegetation in 2022</label>
            <label><input type="radio" name="reading" value="history" /> the two historical readings</label>
          </fieldset>

          <div class="select-pair">
            <label for="history-filter">Historical condition
              <select id="history-filter">
                <option value="all">Both histories</option>
                <option value="open_in_both">Open in 1996 and 2018</option>
                <option value="built_then_open">Built in 1996, open in 2018</option>
              </select>
            </label>
            <label for="vegetation-filter">2022 vegetation response
              <select id="vegetation-filter">
                <option value="all">Every measured response</option>
                <option value="0">Under 20 percent</option>
                <option value="1">20 to under 50 percent</option>
                <option value="2">50 to under 80 percent</option>
                <option value="3">80 percent or more</option>
              </select>
            </label>
          </div>

          <div class="list-heading"><p id="sample-count" role="status" aria-live="polite">14 parcels in view</p><button id="clear-filters" type="button">reset</button></div>
          <p class="list-instruction">Choose an address or a dark-outlined parcel. The list runs from higher to lower vegetation response.</p>
          <div id="parcel-list" class="parcel-list" aria-label="Analysed parcels"></div>
          <p id="no-parcels" class="empty-reading" hidden>No sampled parcels match both choices. Reset the filters to return to all 14.</p>
          <p class="marginal-note">The sample is deliberately selected. These fourteen lots cannot represent the city as a whole.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="surface-reading" class="surface-reading" hidden>
          <h2>A closer kind of record</h2>
          <p>The same vacant-land category contains very different surfaces. These fourteen image fragments keep the shape of each actual parcel.</p>
          <p>Start with two lots whose earlier readings match, then unfold the full sample. Choose a fragment to return to its place on the map.</p>
          <p class="marginal-note">The fragments record the 2022 surface. Field observations will investigate vegetation, maintenance and access.</p>
          <a class="text-action register-download leaf-action" href={url("data/assignment04/field_register.csv")} download>Take the fourteen-lot register</a>
          <p class="register-note">CSV - original measurement precision, source years and parcel identifiers.</p>
        </section>

        <details class="reading-method">
          <summary>the evidence and its limits</summary>
          <div>
            <p><strong>Different dates, different evidence.</strong> 1996 and 2018 are aerial-image observations. 2022 is the vegetation measurement. 2026 is a PLUTO land-use classification, not a new aerial observation.</p>
            <p><strong>Reading the green.</strong> The mapped percentage is the share of valid image pixels with NDVI greater than 0.20. NDVI is calculated as (near infrared − red) ÷ (near infrared + red). The threshold is exploratory.</p>
            <p>Raster summaries include pixels touched by the current parcel boundary. Historical parcel boundaries and small edge effects may differ.</p>
            <p>Two historical snapshots do not prove uninterrupted vacancy. NDVI does not identify trees, biodiversity, cooling, public access, or permanent forest.</p>
            <p>The two sample groups have similar median responses: 63.1 percent and 63.6 percent. This small descriptive sample does not establish that earlier vacancy produces more vegetation.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reading-method sources-detail">
          <summary>sources and credits</summary>
          <div>
            <p><a href="https://data.cityofnewyork.us/City-Government/Primary-Land-Use-Tax-Lot-Output-PLUTO-/64uk-42ks" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NYC Department of City Planning - PLUTO and MapPLUTO 26v2</a>. Administrative land-use records. The 254-lot pilot uses the original matched tax-lot geometry from Assignment 2.</p>
            <p><a href="https://maps.nyc.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NYC Office of Technology and Innovation</a> - aerial imagery from 1996 and 2018.</p>
            <p><a href="https://imagery.geoplatform.gov/iipp/rest/services/NAIP/NAIP_plus/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">USDA NAIP Plus</a> - 2022 four-band imagery. An official image crop was independently checked against the retained raster.</p>
            <p>Geographic source layers and scripted raster analysis come from the earlier course work. This web index is an interactive companion to the final atlas proposal.</p>
            <p><a href={url("assignment04-code-provenance.txt")} target="_blank">Code origins and AI contribution - text file</a><br /><a href="https://github.com/mere0125/astro-maplibre-template" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Project code and data</a></p>
            <p class="credit-line">Mere - November 2026</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <a class="tutorial-back leaf-action" href={url("full_page_map")}>tutorial map</a>
      </aside>

      <main class="field-map-shell" aria-label="Interactive map and selected parcel evidence">
        <div class="map-plane" id="map-plane">
        <div id="assignment-map" class="field-map" aria-label="Map of New York City vacant tax lots"></div>
        <div class="map-caption" id="map-caption"><span class="caption-place" id="caption-place">New York City</span><span id="caption-detail">vacant tax-lot records - 26v2</span></div>
        <div class="map-loading" id="map-loading" role="status">Opening the field index…</div>
        <div class="map-status" id="map-status" role="alert" hidden></div>

        <div class="field-map-tools" aria-label="Map tools">
          <button type="button" id="map-zoom-in" aria-label="Zoom in">+</button>
          <button type="button" id="map-zoom-out" aria-label="Zoom out">−</button>
          <button type="button" id="map-home" aria-label="Return to the selected geographic scale">↺</button>
          <button type="button" id="toggle-legend" aria-label="Show or hide the map key" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="atlas-map-key" class="key-control">key</button>
          <button type="button" id="map-north" class="north-control" aria-label="Reset the map to north"><span>N</span><svg viewBox="0 0 20 25" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 2 17 21 10 17 3 21Z" /></svg></button>
        </div>

        <section class="map-key" id="atlas-map-key" aria-label="Map legend">
          <p class="key-title" id="key-title">vacant land records</p>
          <div id="city-key"><div class="atlas-key-row"><i class="key-patch city-patch"></i><span>MapPLUTO vacant tax lot</span></div><div class="atlas-key-row"><i class="key-window"></i><span>pilot study window</span></div></div>
          <div id="study-key" hidden>
            <div class="vegetation-key" id="vegetation-key">
              <p>Share of valid pixels with NDVI &gt; 0.20</p>
              <div class="atlas-key-row"><i style="--swatch:#eee6cc"></i><span>under 20 percent</span></div>
              <div class="atlas-key-row"><i style="--swatch:#cbd8b7"></i><span>20 to under 50 percent</span></div>
              <div class="atlas-key-row"><i style="--swatch:#98b487"></i><span>50 to under 80 percent</span></div>
              <div class="atlas-key-row"><i style="--swatch:#4c7257"></i><span>80 percent or more</span></div>
              <p class="key-subtitle">Outline - historical snapshots</p>
            </div>
            <div class="atlas-key-row"><i class="key-stroke old-stroke"></i><span>open in 1996 and 2018</span></div>
            <div class="atlas-key-row"><i class="key-stroke recent-stroke"></i><span>built in 1996, open in 2018</span></div>
            <div class="atlas-key-row context-key"><i style="--swatch:#c8d3bb"></i><span>other screened parcels</span></div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="parcel-sheet" id="parcel-sheet" aria-label="Selected parcel evidence" hidden>
          <button id="close-parcel" class="close-parcel" type="button" aria-label="Close parcel evidence">×</button>
          <p class="parcel-heading-note">one close reading</p>
          <h2 id="parcel-address"></h2>
          <p id="parcel-identification" class="parcel-identification"></p>
          <button type="button" class="back-to-folio leaf-action" id="back-to-surfaces" hidden>return to the surface folio</button>
          <div class="record-strip" aria-label="Three dated observations">
            <div><span>1996 - image</span><strong id="status-1996"></strong></div>
            <div><span>2018 - image</span><strong id="status-2018"></strong></div>
            <div><span>2026 - record</span><strong>coded vacant</strong></div>
          </div>
          <div class="parcel-measure"><p><strong id="vegetation-value"></strong><span>of valid parcel pixels above NDVI 0.20 in 2022</span></p><div class="response-track" aria-hidden="true"><span id="response-fill"></span></div><p class="response-detail" id="response-detail"></p></div>
          <div class="image-modes" aria-label="Choose evidence imagery">
            <button type="button" data-evidence="archive" aria-pressed="true">1996 to 2018</button>
            <button type="button" data-evidence="2022" aria-pressed="false">the 2022 surface</button>
          </div>
          <div class="image-pair" id="image-pair">
            <p class="image-loading" id="image-loading" role="status">Loading the dated images…</p>
            <img id="image-back" alt="" />
            <div class="image-front" id="image-front"><img id="image-front-img" alt="" /></div>
            <div class="image-seam" id="image-seam" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <div class="image-label left" id="image-label-left">1996</div>
            <div class="image-label right" id="image-label-right">2018</div>
            <input type="range" id="image-comparison" min="0" max="100" value="50" aria-label="Compare the two dated aerial images" />
          </div>
          <p class="image-caption" id="image-caption">Move the divider to compare the same ground extent. The thin outline locates the present-day parcel.</p>
          <div class="pixel-key" id="pixel-key" hidden><p>pixel NDVI - a different scale from the parcel legend</p><div></div><p><span>−0.2</span><span>0.2</span><span>0.8</span></p></div>
          <p class="parcel-caution">An image reading of the surface - not a survey of trees or habitat.</p>
        </section>
        <p class="map-projection">Web Mercator - EPSG 3857</p>
        </div>

        <article class="surface-folio" id="surface-folio" aria-labelledby="surface-title" hidden>
          <header class="folio-heading">
            <p class="folio-place">East New York - fourteen image readings</p>
            <h2 id="surface-title" tabindex="-1"><span>“vacant”</span><br />in fourteen forms</h2>
            <p class="folio-opening">What a land-use record leaves for us to look at.</p>
          </header>

          <section class="paired-reading" aria-labelledby="pair-title">
            <div class="pair-introduction"><h3 id="pair-title">Two lots with the same earlier readings</h3><p>Both appear open in the 1996 and 2018 images. Both are coded vacant in the 2026 record. Their 2022 surfaces tell very different stories.</p></div>
            <div class="evidence-pair" id="surface-pair"></div>
            <p class="pair-footnote">2022 NAIP true-colour images - identical 450-foot ground contexts. Pale outlines locate the current parcels. These deliberately selected examples are not a controlled comparison or evidence of continuous vacancy.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="specimen-section" aria-labelledby="specimen-title">
            <div class="specimen-heading"><h3 id="specimen-title">The fourteen parcels</h3><p>Current parcel boundaries frame the 2022 image. A shared ground scale keeps their shapes and relative sizes comparable.</p></div>
            <div class="specimen-instructions"><p id="specimen-scale-note">Each image occupies the same ground extent, with grid north at the top.</p></div>
            <fieldset class="specimen-order"><legend>Arrange the collection</legend><label><input type="radio" name="surface-order" value="response" checked /> by measured response</label><label><input type="radio" name="surface-order" value="history" /> by the two histories</label></fieldset>
            <p class="specimen-click-note">Choose a parcel to locate it on the map and read its dated evidence.</p>
            <div class="specimen-collection" id="specimen-collection" aria-live="polite"></div>
          </section>

          <section class="folio-reflection" aria-labelledby="surface-reflection-title">
            <h3 id="surface-reflection-title">What this leaves open</h3>
            <p id="surface-group-summary"></p>
            <p>A vacant-land inventory gives this atlas places to investigate. Historical images and vegetation measurements help choose contrasting cases. Field observation is still needed to establish what grows there, how the ground is maintained, and who can use it.</p>
            <p class="folio-method">The percentage is the share of valid assigned pixels with NDVI greater than 0.20. It measures spectral vegetation response, not tree canopy or habitat quality. Parcel fragments are display resamplings; the measurements use the original raster. Sources: NYC DCP and tax-lot geometry, NYC OTI archival imagery, USDA NAIP 2022. Full methods and credits are in the field notes.</p>
            <div class="folio-actions"><button type="button" class="leaf-action" id="surface-return-map">Return to the map</button><a class="leaf-action" href={url("data/assignment04/field_register.csv")} download>Download the field register</a></div>
          </section>
          <p class="folio-signature">The Temporary Forest - Mere - November 2026</p>
        </article>
      </main>
    </div>
    <script>
      import "../scripts/assignment04";
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
